IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-59. NOUNS of a cross-reference, of a notice's recital and of a printed title. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Economic Competition Law, 5748-1988. It records five items that the texts it read show.
-- (1) A title: the Law carries a new name since 2019, and the old name is still the one in the printed titles of some instruments under it. This is a RECORD, not a defect of the Law.
-- (2) A citation in a fee schedule to a section that the consolidation prints as repealed.
-- (3) A citation in the same fee schedule to a section whose text no longer describes the proceeding the item names.
-- (4) A recital in a fee notice whose two index years differ by two.
-- (5) A citation in a set of regulations to a power in a Law that the consolidation prints as repealed.
-- A citation whose two descriptions differ, a target without the proceeding the citing words name, or two index years that do not differ by one, is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module (`src:` lines are the Law's consolidation, `ext:[fees]`, `ext:[order]` and `ext:[t1964]` lines are the other three consolidations,
-- `ext:[SH ...]` and `ext:[KT ...]` lines are typed from a cropped page image of the official instrument).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `section 28 of the Law, as fee item (a)(3) names it: an appeal against a requirement of the Commissioner`
    `section 28 of the Law, as its consolidation prints it: a repeal marker in place of text`
    `section 30 of the Law, as fee item (b)(5) names it: an application to regulate monopoly actions`
    `section 30 of the Law, as its consolidation prints it: instructions of the Commissioner to a monopolist, and an objection to the Tribunal in subsection (ו)`
    `section 7 of the Law: an application to approve a restrictive arrangement`
    `section 10א of the 1959 Law, as the 1964 regulations name it: the source of the power to make them`
    `the 1959 Law, as section 53 of the Law prints it: repealed`
    `regulation 2 of the 1964 regulations: the delivery of a notice`

-- Three kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest.
-- The second kind is the honest name for the limbs read from a crop: the official page was read, but that no LATER instrument touched the words rests on the consolidation's header.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the text the citing words name stopped being the text in force on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the consolidation prints the named text as repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the target holds a proceeding of the kind the citing words name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a recital`

-- A notice of the Courts Director that changes the amounts prints, in its first operative section, two index readings: the later one and the one it is compared with.
-- The row records the two years as printed; the month is the same in both.
DECLARE `A fee notice recital` HAS
    `the notice is printed in` IS A STRING
    `the month of both indexes printed` IS A STRING
    `the year of the later index printed` IS A NUMBER
    `the year of the earlier index printed` IS A NUMBER
    `the recital was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a printed title`

DECLARE `What a printed title carries` IS ONE OF
    `the words the 2019 rename replaced: ההגבלים העסקיים`
    `the words the 2019 rename put in their place: התחרות הכלכלית`

DECLARE `A printed title` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A STRING
    `the title carries` IS A `What a printed title carries`
    `the title was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

DECLARE `A rename` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A STRING
    `it replaces` IS A `What a printed title carries`
    `by` IS A `What a printed title carries`
    `the rename was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
